 and 58% reach +6 by move 20.","Watch your bishop: it is behind 24% of your lost leads, 1.5\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the dark-squared bishop (67%), landing on f4, e3, g5.","Aim at their bishop: it is behind 19% of their lost leads, 1.2\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the dark-squared bishop (68%). The reply wins it outright 29% of the time. Take it with a bishop.","Material changes hands for you on f6 and f8: build pressure there.","They win material on d4 and e5: keep those squares defended.","Look for the skewer: it appears 1.6\u00d7 as often as usual in this opening."],"similar":[],"family":"Caro-Kann Defense"}